<!--
    A call that stores two arguments through its first parameter immediately
    before passing them to a stripped printf-like helper loses both values.
    onlyOpUse sees the STORE descendants and rejects the esi/edx input trials.

    The other arm calls the same helper with the same constant format pointer
    and recovers all three arguments.  This is stronger evidence than an
    ordinary partial-list sibling: the first argument value identifies the
    same format operation at both sites.

    Phase: P4 call recovery.  The partial-list extension
    (kuna_calleearitylive.rs, always on) uses the equal constant first argument
    as the sibling witness and restores both values.  no_conversion_control
    repeats the call shapes with a plain string and proves that pointer
    equality alone does not lend the longer arity.
-->
